From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yumi-Lab <nicolas@yumi-lab.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fdrv: log the management frame confirm with the driver's own
 macro

rwnx_tx.c holds the only trace_printk() of the two modules we build. A
module that contains one makes the kernel print, when it is loaded:

  ** trace_printk() being used. Allocating extra memory.  **
  ** This means that this is a DEBUG kernel and it is     **
  ** unsafe for production use.                           **

and allocate the trace_printk buffers, on a board with 1 GB of RAM. Seen
on a SmartPi One as soon as aic8800_fdrv is loaded (2026-10-12). Use
AICWFDBG(LOGDEBUG, ...) like the rest of the file: same message, printed
only when the driver's debug level asks for it.
---
 aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c b/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
--- a/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
+++ b/aic8800_fdrv/rwnx_tx.c
@@ -2391,7 +2391,7 @@
 
     /* Update txq and HW queue credits */
     if (sw_txhdr->desc.host.flags & TXU_CNTRL_MGMT) {
-        trace_printk("done=%d retry_required=%d sw_retry_required=%d acknowledged=%d\n",
+        AICWFDBG(LOGDEBUG, "done=%d retry_required=%d sw_retry_required=%d acknowledged=%d\n",
                      rwnx_txst.tx_done, rwnx_txst.retry_required,
                      rwnx_txst.sw_retry_required, rwnx_txst.acknowledged);
 #ifdef CREATE_TRACE_POINTS
